    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW266b2wAzfAJMBjD5JpGuLWE)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent; builds on b09d4e0 (already on `main`).\n- Needs `aerospace-keys.lua` (Caps Lock layer) to load first; it does, in `init.lua`.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Replaces the global Cmd+Ctrl+Option+H leader (and its Cmd+Option+Space comment) in `hammerspoon/.config/hammerspoon/devonthink.lua`.\n- `Caps+x`: Tools > Annotate > Highlight Text.\n- `Caps+c`: next colour (Yellow, Red, Green, Blue), then highlight again.\n- Keys act only when DEVONthink 3 or 4 is frontmost; elsewhere they do nothing.\n- The activation watcher is removed: highlight mode starts only when you press the key.\n\n## Why these keys\n\n- The layer never reaches Emacs and uses no Option, Cmd+Space or Ctrl+Space chord.\n- `x` and `c` are free in the layer (used: h/j/k/l, 1-9, a, b, d, e, m, t, w, `/`, `,`, tab, return, escape).\n- A native App Shortcut did not work, so no DEVONthink-side setup is needed.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Reload Hammerspoon: no error in the console.\n- [x] In DEVONthink with a PDF open, select text, hold Caps and press `x`: text is highlighted.\n- [x] Press Caps+`c` repeatedly: colour cycles Yellow, Red, Green, Blue and highlights.\n- [x] Switch to DEVONthink: nothing is highlighted automatically.\n- [x] In another app, Caps+`x` and Caps+`c` do nothing.\n- [x] Existing Caps+h/j/k/l and workspace keys still work.\n- [x] If \"Menu item not found\" appears, check the exact Tools > Annotate and Format > Highlight Color names in DEVONthink.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCTb5QFPFZUd9wzRgq)_",
